# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Names each fresh summon after its kind: lych, mumi, thral, wytch and so on.
# The pet bars and nameplates then show what is out, and a summon answers to its name in
# a pet command.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ config
#
#   config__summon_range
#      How far the block looks for summons, the whole screen, so a summon that lagged
#      behind is still named.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__summon_range 18


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ state
#
#   var__summon_seen
#      Scratch: the match the walk is looking at, copied out of its alias for inlist.
#
#   var__fresh_summon
#      Scratch: the first own summon not named yet, 0 for none.
#
#   var__summon_kind
#      Scratch: the kind read off its label, as an index into list__summon_kinds. 99 for a
#      kind the list does not have.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! var__summon_seen 0
@setvar! var__fresh_summon 0
@setvar! var__summon_kind 99


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ setup
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The summons this script already named, by serial. Emptied at every start, so a summon a
# previous run could not name gets another try.
if not listexists 'list__named_summons'
    createlist 'list__named_summons'
endif
clearlist 'list__named_summons'

# The names, in the order the kinds are read below. A list, because a variable cannot hold a
# word, and foreach hands an entry to rename as it is. Rebuilt on every start. Each is spelt
# so it does not hold the creature's own word: the server refused "mummy" with "That name is
# unacceptable." (2026-10-10), and RunUO's name check also refuses words such as "mage".
if not listexists 'list__summon_kinds'
    createlist 'list__summon_kinds'
endif
clearlist 'list__summon_kinds'
pushlist 'list__summon_kinds' 'knite'
pushlist 'list__summon_kinds' 'magi'
pushlist 'list__summon_kinds' 'lych'
pushlist 'list__summon_kinds' 'mumi'
pushlist 'list__summon_kinds' 'thral'
pushlist 'list__summon_kinds' 'wytch'
pushlist 'list__summon_kinds' 'zombi'
pushlist 'list__summon_kinds' 'gost'
pushlist 'list__summon_kinds' 'skelly'
pushlist 'list__summon_kinds' 'ghul'
pushlist 'list__summon_kinds' 'rotter'


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ loop
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # SUMMON NAMES
    #
    # A fresh summon still wears its stock name, "a lich" and so on, and is renamed to a
    # spelling of its kind that the server takes: lych, mumi, thral, wytch, zombi, gost,
    # skelly, knite, magi, ghul, rotter. Nothing here casts or opens a cursor, so it runs
    # engaged or not, one rename per run. A clock group such as every
    # interval__housekeeping keeps it off most passes.
    #
    # Summons are found by body id, because Razor may keep the old name cached after a
    # rename and the body never changes. The kind is read off the label once, before the
    # rename, and its name comes out of list__summon_kinds by index. A renamed summon
    # still matches its body, so its serial goes into list__named_summons once its kind is
    # known, and the walk skips it from then on. The list is emptied at every start and
    # once no follower is left. The noto test keeps own summons only: they read friend,
    # and another player's summon reads innocent unless that player is guild or allied.
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    if followers > 0
        @setvar! var__fresh_summon 0

        # Bodies. Lich 24 and ancient mummy 158 read off >info, vampire thrall 722 and rag
        # witch 740 from the old bard-necro follower cache, and the Summon Creature undead
        # pool as far as the stock client art goes, zombie 3, ghost 26, skeleton 50, 56, 57,
        # skeletal knight 147, skeletal mage 148, ghoul 153, rotting corpse 155. Skeletal
        # Fiend, skeletal marksman and rotting flesh are Outlands bodies: read theirs with
        # >info when one is out and add the number here, and its name below. The plain
        # elementals and daemon a summon gives without Vengeful Spirit, 9 and 13 to 16, are
        # left out: other mages' elementals on screen were taken for our own, a guildmate's
        # among them, which the noto test cannot tell apart.
        # Walk every match, not just the first: this Razor hands back the same mobile on
        # every call. Each rejected match is ignored for the rest of the walk, and the
        # ignore list is emptied again so the rest of the loop sees everything.
        while findtype 24|158|722|740|3|26|50|56|57|147|148|153|155 ground -1 -1 config__summon_range as alias__fresh_summon
            @setvar! var__summon_seen alias__fresh_summon

            if not inlist 'list__named_summons' var__summon_seen
                if not dead alias__fresh_summon and noto alias__fresh_summon != "hostile" and noto alias__fresh_summon != "criminal" and noto alias__fresh_summon != "enemy" and noto alias__fresh_summon != "murderer" and noto alias__fresh_summon != "innocent"
                    # The label is read here, while the alias is bound, the way every getlabel
                    # in this repository reads it. A phrase of each stock name, in the order of
                    # list__summon_kinds, in either case.
                    getlabel alias__fresh_summon label__fresh_summon
                    @setvar! var__summon_kind 99
                    if "skeletal knight" in label__fresh_summon or "Skeletal Knight" in label__fresh_summon
                        @setvar! var__summon_kind 0
                    elseif "skeletal mage" in label__fresh_summon or "Skeletal Mage" in label__fresh_summon
                        @setvar! var__summon_kind 1
                    elseif "lich" in label__fresh_summon or "Lich" in label__fresh_summon
                        @setvar! var__summon_kind 2
                    elseif "mummy" in label__fresh_summon or "Mummy" in label__fresh_summon
                        @setvar! var__summon_kind 3
                    elseif "thrall" in label__fresh_summon or "Thrall" in label__fresh_summon
                        @setvar! var__summon_kind 4
                    elseif "witch" in label__fresh_summon or "Witch" in label__fresh_summon
                        @setvar! var__summon_kind 5
                    elseif "zombie" in label__fresh_summon or "Zombie" in label__fresh_summon
                        @setvar! var__summon_kind 6
                    elseif "ghost" in label__fresh_summon or "Ghost" in label__fresh_summon
                        @setvar! var__summon_kind 7
                    elseif "skeleton" in label__fresh_summon or "Skeleton" in label__fresh_summon
                        @setvar! var__summon_kind 8
                    elseif "ghoul" in label__fresh_summon or "Ghoul" in label__fresh_summon
                        @setvar! var__summon_kind 9
                    elseif "rotting corpse" in label__fresh_summon or "Rotting Corpse" in label__fresh_summon
                        @setvar! var__summon_kind 10
                    endif

                    if var__summon_kind != 99
                        @setvar! var__fresh_summon alias__fresh_summon
                        break
                    endif

                    # A label without a known kind (not loaded yet on a fresh summon, or a
                    # stock name this table lacks) is passed over and read again on the next
                    # run, so the summons after it still get their names. The Journal shows
                    # it, so a missing kind can be added.
                    if config__sysmsg = 1
                        sysmsg "Summon name: no known kind in its label: {{label__fresh_summon}}" 88
                    endif
                endif
            endif

            @ignore alias__fresh_summon
        endwhile

        @clearignore

        # The rag witch's body number is not confirmed: 740 came from an old script and no
        # rag witch was found by it (2026-10-10). So when the bodies give nothing, it is also
        # looked up by its stock name, which findtype matches as well. Once >info gives its
        # body, add that to the line above and drop this walk.
        if var__fresh_summon = 0
            while findtype "a rag witch" ground -1 -1 config__summon_range as alias__fresh_summon
                @setvar! var__summon_seen alias__fresh_summon

                if not inlist 'list__named_summons' var__summon_seen
                    if not dead alias__fresh_summon and noto alias__fresh_summon != "hostile" and noto alias__fresh_summon != "criminal" and noto alias__fresh_summon != "enemy" and noto alias__fresh_summon != "murderer" and noto alias__fresh_summon != "innocent"
                        @setvar! var__fresh_summon alias__fresh_summon
                        @setvar! var__summon_kind 5

                        if config__sysmsg = 1
                            sysmsg "Summon name: a rag witch found by its name, not its body. Read its body with >info." 88
                        endif
                        break
                    endif
                endif

                @ignore alias__fresh_summon
            endwhile

            @clearignore
        endif

        if var__fresh_summon != 0
            pushlist 'list__named_summons' var__fresh_summon

            # The loop name pet_name is a word no other name here contains, in case Razor
            # puts the entry in by text.
            foreach pet_name in list__summon_kinds
                if index = var__summon_kind
                    @rename var__fresh_summon pet_name

                    if config__chatty = 1
                        overhead "[ name, {{pet_name}} ]" 209 var__fresh_summon
                    endif
                endif
            endfor
        endif
    else
        clearlist 'list__named_summons'
    endif
